<title>USA: Converse stake cut by Vinik group.</title>
<headline>Converse stake cut by Vinik group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by Boston investor Jeffrey Vinik said Tuesday it cuts its stake in Converse Inc to 1,252,000 common shares or 7.5 percent from 8.9 percent held previously.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said its latest transactions include a net 246,500 common shares sold between January 27 and March 4 at prices ranging from $15.2343 to $26.6820 per share.</p>
<p>Converse, based in Boston, Mass., makes athletic footwear and apparel.</p>
